[#:seon.task{:name "one-weighted-cache-under-a-memory-cap"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "About fifteen defonce caches each carry a code-constant entry bound and no byte cap (seon.db arity-commit 92.6 MB, projection 12.8 MB, arity-base 9.0 MB; seon.sci.eval base-context 27.4 MB, program-identity, refusal-recording; seon.test.runner reach-holders 16.7 MB; the build-projection memos). Owner rulings: every cache configurable, a library not a hand-rolled cache, one fixed memory cap. Recommended: one Caffeine cache keyed [cache-id key] with maximumWeight from one byte dial and a weigher recorded at insert (~60 lines, roughly net neutral)."
             :must-read #{seon.db/carried-projection seon.sci.eval/base-ctx seon.test.runner/reach-memberships}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/mem-idle-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md"}} #:seon.task{:name "non-reach-kinds-weigh-three-to-seven-times-their-retained-bytes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "After the reach kinds were refit (cache-weight lane, 2026-10-09), the next largest seon.cache kinds still charge several times what an object-graph walk of their retained keys and values measures on default: :seon.sci.eval/loaded-digests 22.2 MB charged vs 8.1 MB (15 entries), :seon.task/tasks-tx 21.0 vs 7.0 MB (2), :seon.fn/population-targets 17.7 vs 2.4 MB (2), :seon.task/task-basis 9.6 vs 4.0 MB (1), :seon.task/file-grammar 8.8 vs 1.2 MB (1), :seon.cluster/derivation-world 9.7 vs 2.1 MB (1); leaves counted, so the true gap is larger where strings are shared. Refit each owner's weigher from counts the value has, with a measurement row and a calibration-test row like the reach kinds'. Done when each kind's charge is within 1.25x of its measured retention. Root cause found 2026-10-12 (restart audit, ~41 MB of the 512 MB budget): `seon.task/task-basis`, `seon.task/tasks-tx`, `seon.task/tasks-tx-in` (`:seon.task/file-grammar`) and `seon.cluster/derivation-keys` (`:seon.cluster/derivation-world`) weigh `schema/declaration-projection-bytes-per-form` x the number of projection forms, but that map is the KEY, shared with the projection and already charged under `:seon.schema/declaration-projection`; the values are one digest, a tx vector or a digest per form. Weigh the value (counts of what it holds), never the key. `:seon.task/file-grammar` also never hits (it caches `(seon.id/digest 64 [forms])` only on a `tasks-tx` miss): delete the lookup and digest inline, or key `file-declarations` by the projection content identity. The red first test is `seon.cache-test/a-kinds-weight-counts-its-value-not-its-key`: for a `tasks-tx` result and a `task-basis` result over the same projection, the weights differ by their values and a larger projection adds nothing."
             :must-read #{seon.cache/lookup seon.sci.eval/loaded-digests seon.task/tasks-tx seon.task/task-basis seon.task/tasks-tx-in seon.cluster/derivation-keys seon.fn/population-targets}
             :evidence #{"bench/seon/cache_kind_measurement.edn" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/restart-audit/cache-hits.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-presence-probe-counts-no-miss"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.cache/settle!` counts a miss for every `seon.cache/lookup` claim, so the get-if-present idiom `(seon.cache/lookup kind key (constantly 0) (constantly nil))` and the put idiom `(constantly value)` count misses that did no work: `seon.cluster/stored-derivation-schema-keys` (`:seon.cluster/file-schema-keys` shows 1,080 misses = 2 x 540 for 540 derivations) and `seon.health/derived` (`:seon.health/reads` and `:seon.health/derived`) inflate the `seon.cache/status` counters this system steers by. Add one non-counting read to `seon.cache` (a completed entry's value or nil, the Caffeine `getIfPresent` that `seon.cache/retained` already reads through) and call it at those two owners, or give each file one lookup whose derive derefs a shared delay of the batch pull. Proof: `seon.cache-test/a-presence-probe-counts-no-miss` (the implementer writes first): after the probe on an absent key `(:misses (seon.cache/status))` for the kind is 0, after the real lookup 1; and `seon.cluster-test` asserts a 540-file derivation counts 540 misses, not 1,080."
             :must-read #{seon.cache/lookup seon.cache/retained seon.cache/status seon.cluster/stored-derivation-schema-keys seon.health/derived}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/restart-audit/cache-hits.md"}}
]
